cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Rift or the Rift Observatory data in your research, please cite
  it as below.
title: "Rift: statistically rigorous drift detection for LLM endpoints"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Rift contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shahcolate/rift"
url: "https://github.com/shahcolate/rift"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - behavioral drift
  - regression testing
  - model monitoring
abstract: >-
  Rift detects behavioral regressions between LLM model versions and monitors
  live endpoints for drift. It pairs eval-suite runs with exact McNemar /
  paired-t significance tests, bootstrap confidence intervals,
  Benjamini-Hochberg correction, pre-registered primary endpoints, and a
  self-test that measures the drift gate's own false-positive rate. Server
  fingerprints are captured on every completion to detect silent model swaps,
  and every cost claim carries a paired-bootstrap confidence interval.
